{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The wired earbuds feel useful as a compact alternative to my larger headphones for listening on my laptop; they fit a use I already have.",
    "The HDMI cable fits my history of connecting equipment, although owning a cable already means I would need a specific reason to buy another."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming sticks do not help with the desk and networking tasks reflected in my recent purchases. My Raspberry Pi project alone does not mean I want another streaming device.",
    "The tablets, voice assistant, smart plug, and portable speaker each need a purpose I have not shown. Reading on a Kindle, using headphones, and working on hardware projects do not automatically create those needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any electronic device, regardless of what I would use it for.",
    "My Amazon-branded purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest more Amazon devices, even though those purchases served different practical purposes."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest purchases connect around a practical computer setup: wired networking, cable organization, equipment cleaning, carrying a laptop, and storing headphones.",
    "What I already own matters: another HDMI cable needs a concrete benefit, while compact wired earbuds offer a different way to use audio equipment I already enjoy."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognize my interest in electronics but miss how strongly my current choices depend on a specific computer-related task or useful addition to equipment I already own."
}"}
